# Shipwright guardrails (static fallback)

This rule mirrors critical guardrails when hook injection is unreliable. Fail-closed enforcement lives in
the `beforeSubmitPrompt` hook (`before-submit-guardrails.py`).

- Route memory ops through `memory-preflight` / `providers/<memory.provider>.md` — never call Recallium directly.
- Never store raw transcripts or secrets in memory.
- **Broker-only secret access** — resolve credentials only through `credentials.resolver` / adapter brokers and
  `credentials.send_path`; never read tokens from config bodies, selector files, or ambient env outside an
  explicitly declared `environment` backend entry.
- **Fail-closed scope enforcement** — `allowedRepos`, `allowedProjectIds`, and `allowedEndpoints` on selector
  entries are mandatory; resolution refuses out-of-scope remotes, project ids, and endpoints.
- CI readiness: run `scripts/check-gate.py` — never hand-roll a green verdict.
- `sw-` commands only for this plugin's workflow surface.
